    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">C010 - Pier Cap Design</paragraph>
    <section name="WorkingNotes" capture="False" hide="true">
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#43505C">Working notes (hidden; not part of the submitted calculation): how this edition was produced, its tool status and the open bookkeeping items.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Distilled from Pier Cap Design 10-20.html (generated 2026-10-20T17:49:55+00:00); same case (canonical SHA-256 868e96bca964) and C005 formula set (327838126d06) as the report; FBMP Pier_Fixed.XML (bb73e6ada6cf); cap notebook package 71ba1ddfc4ef. Blockpad edition written by scripts/build_cap_bpad.py from the same case; every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the cap tool to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes note: inherited sectional relations of the cap tool (C005 formula set 327838126d06).</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Tool status: CHECK FAILURES — revise the trial cage or section.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Service III (D-007) and fatigue remain pending.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Failing checks not recomputed here (tool): End U grid · pile envelope clearance: Conservative square pile envelope includes the current horizontal placement allowance, pile embedment and required clear gap, enlarged by bar radius. Review shape-specific and fabrication tolerances separately.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">The tool reports 67 PENDING items: 2 Service III and fatigue; 3 FDOT covers; 4 D-regions, end regions and the end grid; 58 actual-cage prerequisites behind the distilled checks (anchorage and closure, splices, load path).</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Detailing and geometry flags: 50 pass, as reported by the tool.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A ✓ status covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. Recalculate in Blockpad after any input change.</paragraph>
    </section>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Project: D2 I-95 Pedestrian Bridge.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Design Guidelines, January 2026, 4.1.4A–C.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6">Inputs are highlighted amber; results are the green tables.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">1. Scope</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Computed here: sectional flexure, minimum steel, strain and Service I crack control in regions N (top steel), P (bottom steel at the piles) and B (bottom steel with the added span bars); the shear depth; actual-cage shear, longitudinal tension, torsion screen and minimum transverse steel at the governing stations found by the station search of the cap analysis; the governing transverse spacing; face shrinkage and temperature steel; skin steel; and the governing hook development.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Taken from the cap analysis and not recomputed here: the station search itself, the intersected-leg window areas and the developed (credited) steel areas (shown as inputs), the detailing and geometry flags, transverse anchorage, the end grid and the D-regions.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4">• Service III is not applicable to this cap; fatigue is not evaluated in this calculation.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">2. Inputs</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="3" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True">Geometry and materials</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="b = 48 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>b = 48 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>cap width</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="h = 36 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>h = 36 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>cap depth</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="C_t = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>C_t = 3 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>top clear cover to the hoop</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="C_b = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>C_b = 3 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>bottom clear cover to the hoop</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="C_s = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>C_s = 3 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>side clear cover to the hoop</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="fc = 5.5 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>fc = 5.5 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>concrete strength</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="fy = 60 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>fy = 60 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>steel yield strength</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="Es = 29000 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>Es = 29000 ksi</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>steel modulus</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_f = 0.9" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_f = 0.9</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>flexure φ</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_v = 0.9" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_v = 0.9</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>shear φ</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_e = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_e = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>crack-control exposure factor</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ = 1</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>density factor</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_a = 0.9" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_a = 0.9</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>axial φ, 5.7.3.5</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="L_cap = 230 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>L_cap = 230 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>cap length (cap analysis)</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="s_proj = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="False" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>s_proj = 12 in</expbody></dynexp><break type="tab"/>project spacing limit, face steel</paragraph>
