    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Figure 3. Demand/capacity ratio of each check (stems) against the 1.0 limit. The stems are live formulas of the check ratios: a stem turns red when its ratio passes 1.0.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Check numbers: 1–3 flexure (N, P, B); 4–6 minimum steel (N, P, B); 7–9 tension-controlled strain (N, P, B); 10–12 Service I (N, P, B); 13 shear at S; 14 longitudinal tension at N; 15 longitudinal tension at P; 16 longitudinal tension at B; 17 minimum transverse steel at M; 18 transverse spacing; 19 face steel area, largest; 20 face bar spacing, largest; 21 hook development.</paragraph>
  </report>
